3. Components downloaded at runtime (not shipped)
-------------------------------------------------

LDM does not ship yt-dlp or deno. After the user agrees (first-use prompt, "ldm tools
install", or the Tools page in the GUI), LDM downloads the official release files from GitHub
into the user's data directory and verifies them before use.
* yt-dlp: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp. The Unlicense (public domain); its release
  binaries bundle components under their own licenses (see the yt-dlp repository).
  - Verification: SHA-256 from the release's SHA2-256SUMS, plus the GPG signature
    SHA2-256SUMS.sig when gpg is installed.
  - The signing key that LDM trusts is the yt-dlp release key that the yt-dlp project
    publishes in its repository (public.key) and README. LDM embeds only that public key
    (crates/ldm-core/src/keys/yt-dlp-signing.asc) and pins its fingerprint in
    crates/ldm-core/src/tools.rs (AC0CBBE6848D6A873464AF4E57CF65933B5A7581). It is a third
    party's public key and is reproduced unmodified for verification only.
* deno: https://github.com/denoland/deno. MIT License. Verified by the SHA-256 file published
  with the release, or by a checksum pinned in LDM; without either, LDM refuses to install it.
* Extractors, site rules and media are fetched from websites at the user's request. Their
  terms are the user's responsibility.

